WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.814
From streaming images and synchronized IMU. we estimate the camera's metric trajectory.

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:15.600
Frozen LingBot-Map supplies geometry. VIStream integrates calibrated inertial motion to follow the path more closely.

3
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.768
The visual backbone stays frozen. A motion expert supplies visual inertial estimates.

4
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.065
Camera alignment and persistent scale connect valid motion increments. while visual motion bridges interruptions.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:40.300
Watch both methods on the same difficult sequence. The reference. support. and metric scale are shared.

6
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:58.780
Repeated turns reveal the same pattern in a second recorded example. The orange path stays closer to ground truth.

7
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:16.474
The input is a real camera stream. with natural viewpoint and lighting changes.

8
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:27.496
These unsmoothed error curves follow both complete sequences. using one fixed rigid alignment.

9
00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:50.794
In these two historical examples. trajectory error falls from five point nine three to zero point three two metres. and from two point six three to zero point two nine.

10
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.321
VIStream. Frozen geometry. Calibrated motion. Visual inertial SLAM.
